-- title:
--   Supersingular DVR, affine chart and q+1 nodes at level q
-- statement:
--   Notation. $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`; for a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $\kappa$ denotes its residue field. For fields $K\subseteq F$, a `Place K F` is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $F$, and a principal ideal ring; `P.ord f` is minus the logarithm of the associated adic valuation of $f$, and `P.evalAt f` is the element of $K$ obtained from the residue of $f$ when $f$ lies in the valuation subring (and $0$ otherwise). `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` is the subfield of `LaurentSeries ℚ` generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the series `qExpand ℚ d jq` for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $M'$, where `jq` is the $q$-expansion of $j$; `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is the subfield of `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise images `coeffEmb` of that field; `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` is the subfield of `LaurentSeries κ` generated over $\kappa$ by `jqModC κ` and `jqNModC κ M'`; and `fieldBar q M'` is `xHFunctionFieldBar (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ for $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$.
--
--   Data and hypotheses. Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, that is, $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ which, by `hW`, consists exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' κ`: those $w$ for which the structure map $\kappa\to$ (residue field of $w$) is surjective, for which `IsAffineGeomPlace κ M' w` holds, and for which the value `w.evalAt (jGeomGen κ M')` of the $j$-generator lies in `ssJSet q κ`. The hypothesis `hle` asserts `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`. Let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` relative to $A$ with target `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective ring homomorphism `R₀.residue` onto the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal of `R₀.integers`, a map `R₀.placeMap` on places preserving degrees, the compatibilities that a constant of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `R₀.integers` exactly when it lies in $A$ and that its residue is the image of its residue in $\kappa$, the scaling property that every nonzero $f$ admits $c\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $cf$ in `R₀.integers` of nonzero residue, and compatibility of divisors with `R₀.placeMap`. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires in addition that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally let $s\in W$.
--
--   Small-field data (`k₀`, `π₀`, `hπ`, `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres`, `hκ`): an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$ such that the contraction $A\cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, is a henselian local ring, and has algebraically closed residue field, and such that every $a\in A$ differs from some $c\in k_0$ with $c\in A$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   Auxiliary constants (`ℓ`, `hℓ`, `hℓ3`, `hℓq`, `hℓM'`, `ζ₀`, `hζ₀`, `ϖt`, `hϖtA`, `hϖt`): a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$, an element $\zeta_0\in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and an element $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   Base layer (`Kb`, `hKb`, `Ab`, `hAb`, `ϖb`, `hϖb`, `hϖb0`): an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K_b=\bot$, a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ whose elements are exactly those lying in $A$, and a nonzero $\varpi_b\in A_b$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   Conclusion. Equip `fieldBar q M'` with the $k_0$-algebra structure coming from $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}\to$ `fieldBar q M'`. Then for every intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ which consists exactly of those $f$ all of whose Laurent coefficients (as a series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) lie in $k_0$, there exists a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ with the following properties.
--
--   (1) For $x\in k_0$: $x\in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (2) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   (3) The image of $\pi_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (4) ($W_0$ lies over $s$.) For every $g\in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose coefficientwise image lies in `R₀.integers`, such that $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}(g)$ at every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}(j)$, and such that `R₀.residue` of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$: the image of $g$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $F_0$, its class lies in $W_0$, and for every $c\in k_0$ with $c\in A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals `s.evalAt` of `R₀.residue` of $g$, the difference of the class of $g$ and the image of $c$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (5) (Level stability.) For every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$), every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\subseteq SL(2,\mathbb Z)$ and every $f\in F_0$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` $\in F_0$: $f\in W_0$ if and only if `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` $\in W_0$. Here `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` is the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra automorphism of `fieldBar q M'` singled out by the predicate `IsLevelAutBar q M' ζ γ`, which prescribes its effect on quotients of $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ in terms of the slash action by `conjElem q γ`, normalised through the embeddings sending $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$ (and is the identity if no such automorphism exists).
--
--   (6) (Affine chart.) There exist a subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` and an $A_b$-algebra structure on $B$ such that:
--
--   (6a) the structure map $A_b\to B$ is the inclusion $A_b\subseteq K_b\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}\to$ `fieldBar q M'`;
--
--   (6b) $B$ is contained in the compositum of the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_b$ and of $F_0$;
--
--   (6c) every element of that compositum is of the form $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $h\ne0$;
--
--   (6d) $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$, and $B/(\varpi_b)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$;
--
--   (6e) every $f\in B$ lies in $F_0$ and its class lies in $W_0$;
--
--   (6f) the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ is prime;
--
--   (6g) an element $f\in F_0$ lies in $W_0$ exactly when $f=g/h$ for some $g,h\in B$ with $h$ not divisible by the image of $\varpi_b$;
--
--   (6h) the image of $j$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $B$;
--
--   (6i) $B$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$;
--
--   (6j) there exists $b\in F_0$ with $b\in B$ such that $b\notin V$ for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which contracts to $A\cap k_0$ on $k_0$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal whenever $\pi_0\in V$, contains the class of $j$ (which then lies in $F_0$), and is such that for every monic polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ with all coefficients in $A$ the value $p(j)$ is a unit at $V$;
--
--   (6k) for every $s'\in W$ with $s'\ne s$ there exists $b\in F_0$ with $b\in B$ such that $b\notin V$ for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which contracts to $A\cap k_0$ on $k_0$ and satisfies the condition (4) with $V$ and $s'$ in place of $W_0$ and $s$;
--
--   (6l) (Drinfeld quotient.) For every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, assuming [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of `MvPolynomial (Fin 2) κ` by `drinfeldPoly q κ - 1`) is a domain, and for every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q`, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) — the fixed field inside the fraction field of `CoordRing q κ` of the subgroup generated by the actions of the elements $(1,\zeta')$, $\zeta'\in C_s$, inside `hSubgroup q`, the kernel of the character $(\gamma,u)\mapsto\det\gamma\cdot u^{q+1}$ on $GL_2(\mathbb Z/q)\times\mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$ — such that: the cardinality of $C_s$ is $2\cdot$`placeWidthChar q M' s` (which for $q\ge5$ is `jWidth` of the $j$-value at $s$ divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s`); the kernel of $\rho$ is the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$; $\rho$ sends the image of $a\in A_b$ to the image of the residue of $a$ under $\kappa\to$ `quotField q κ Cs`; every element of `quotField q κ Cs` is of the form $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$ with $g,h\in B$ and $\rho(h)\ne0$; the image of $\rho$ consists exactly of those elements lying in the image of `CoordRing q κ` in the Drinfeld function field; and for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ such that $(\mathrm{red}_q\gamma,1)$ lies in `hSubgroup q`, and every $f\in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹ f` $\in B$, one has $\rho($`levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹ f`$)=$ `hFunctionFieldAction q κ` at $(\mathrm{red}_q\gamma,1)$ applied to $\rho(f)$;
--
--   (6m) (Nodes.) The image of $j$ lies in `R₀.integers`, its `R₀`-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the series `jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q` (the image of `jqModC` under `qExpand _ q`) lies in `fieldBar q M'`, there is $a_0\in k_0$ with $a_0\in A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ satisfies $(\mathrm{res}\,a_0)^q=$ `s.evalAt` of the `R₀`-residue of $j$, and there is a finite set `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$ such that:
--
--   • `nodes` has exactly $q+1$ elements;
--
--   • (common chart) there is a subring $B_c$ of $F_0$ which is the subring generated by the image of $\{x\in k_0: x\in A\}$ together with a finite subset $T$ of $F_0$, such that every $O\in$ `nodes` contains $B_c$ and, for every $O\in$ `nodes`, an element $f\in F_0$ lies in $O$ exactly when $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B_c$ and $h$ a unit of $O$;
--
--   • for every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $O\in$ `nodes` there is $O'\in$ `nodes` such that, for $f\in F_0$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` $\in F_0$, one has $f\in O$ iff `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ f` $\in O'$;
--
--   • for every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` and all $O,O'\in$ `nodes` there is $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with the same equivalence, so the level automorphisms act transitively on `nodes`;
--
--   • for distinct $O,O'\in$ `nodes` there is $f$ lying in both which is not a unit of $O$ but is a unit of $O'$;
--
--   • every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which contracts to $A\cap k_0$ on $k_0$ and satisfies condition (4) with $V$ in place of $W_0$ either contains $B$ (every $f\in B$ lies in $F_0$ with class in $V$) or dominates some node: there is $O\in$ `nodes` with $O\subseteq V$ and with every non-unit of $O$ lying in the maximal ideal of $V$;
--
--   • for every $O\in$ `nodes`: $O\subseteq W_0$; $O$ is a local Noetherian ring; $x\in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $O$, for $x\in k_0$; every $f\in O$ differs from the image of some $x\in k_0$ with $x\in A$ by a non-unit of $O$; and there is $E_0\ge1$ together with the following data. First, there is $v\in k_0$ with $v$ and $v^{-1}$ in $A$ and $\pi_0^{E_0}=\varpi_t^{\,2\cdot\mathrm{placeWidthChar}(q,M',s)}\,v$. Next, $\pi_0$ lies in $O$, and there are $c_x,c_y\in O$, a unit $u$ of $O$, a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto `UVCrossingModel` of the adic completion $\widehat W$ of $A\cap k_0$ at its maximal ideal at the parameter $\hat\pi_0^{\,E_0}$ — that is, `MvPowerSeries (Fin 2)` $\widehat W$ modulo $X_0X_1-\hat\pi_0^{\,E_0}$ — and units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of this crossing model, such that: $c_xc_y=\pi_0^{E_0}u$ in $O$; $\iota$ carries the image of each constant $x\in k_0$ with $x\in A$ and image in $O$ to the corresponding constant of the crossing model; $\iota(c_x)=\gamma_U\cdot U$ and $\iota(c_y)=\gamma_V\cdot V$; $c_y$ lies in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal; and $c_x$, when in $W_0$, is not in the maximal ideal of $W_0$. Furthermore (Hasse datum at the node) the difference of `jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q` and the image of $a_0$ lies in $F_0$ and in $O$, and there are $e\ge1$ and a unit $w_V$ of the crossing model with $\iota$ of that difference equal to $w_V\cdot V^e$. Furthermore there is a valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ with: $O\subseteq W_x$; $W_x$ contracting to $A\cap k_0$ on $k_0$; $W_x$ a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $\pi_0$; an element $t\in W_x$ such that for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ with all coefficients in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ then every coefficient of $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$; $c_x$ in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ whenever $c_x\in W_x$, and $c_y$ outside it whenever $c_y\in W_x$; and, for every $g\in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose coefficientwise image lies in `R₀.integers` and which is regular at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $j$ is regular, the class of $g$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_x$, lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ exactly when its `R₀`-residue vanishes, and, if its `R₀`-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, lies in $O$ and differs by a non-unit of $O$ from the image of every $c\in k_0$ with $c\in A$, image in $O$, whose residue equals `s.evalAt` of that `R₀`-residue. Finally there is a subring $B_x$ of $F_0$ with: every $f\in B_x$ has image in $B$ and lies in $O$; every $f\in B_x$ satisfies $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}(f)$ at every place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}(j)$; an element $f\in F_0$ lies in $O$ exactly when $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B_x$ and $h$ a unit of $O$; every $f\in F_0$ is of the form $g/h$ with $g,h\in B_x$, $h\ne0$; $B_x$ is the subring generated by the image of $\{x\in k_0:x\in A\}$ together with a finite subset of $F_0$; and there is $b\in B_x$ such that $b\notin V$ for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which contracts to $A\cap k_0$ on $k_0$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal whenever $\pi_0\in V$, contains the class of $j$, is such that $p(j)$ is a unit at $V$ for every monic polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ with coefficients in $A$, and does not contain all of $O$.
--
--   This is the level-$q$ stage in the construction of a semistable chart, with its $q+1$ nodes, on the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ at a supersingular point $s$ of the level-$M'$ curve over the residue field of $A$: it produces simultaneously the discrete valuation ring $W_0$ lying over $s$, an $A_b$-chart $B$ whose reduction modulo $\varpi_b$ is a Drinfeld quotient curve with poles at the remaining supersingular points, a common finitely generated chart for the $q+1$ nodes with its transitive level action, and at each node a $UV$-crossing presentation of the completion in which the rescaled moduli function $j(q\tau)-a_0$ is a monomial in $V$. It is proved from [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_of_levelField`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_of_levelField), which carries the same hypotheses together with further separation data, and is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_nodes_of_levelField`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_nodes_of_levelField) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_nodes_of_levelField`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_nodes_of_levelField).
